---
source: crates/paper-cli/tests/help.rs
expression: "env.paper(&[\"help\"]).stdout"
---
Version control for researchers

Usage: paper [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  init      Make a folder a paper project, or adopt an existing git repository
  save      Save the draft (or only some files) with a message
  history   List saves, newest first
  show      Show one save: metadata, changed files and their diffs
  status    List the unsaved changes in the draft
  diff      Compare two points, or the last save and the draft
  config    Read or change paper's settings
  activity  List what you and paper did to the project, newest first
  undo      Take back the last thing you or paper did, files included
  redo      Bring back what you just undid
  gc        Trim the undo history to a recent window, so git can reclaim old drafts and undone work
  ignore    Stop tracking files or folders, even saved ones; with no arguments, list the ignore rules
  unignore  Track files or folders again: remove their ignore rule, or add an exception
  help      Explain a command or a topic (try `paper help large-files`)
  restore   Put files back the way they were at a point

Options:
  -C <PATH>            Run as if started in this folder
      --json           Machine-readable output
      --no-snapshot    Skip the automatic snapshot
  -q, --quiet          Print only errors
  -v, --verbose        Add git terms in parentheses
      --color <COLOR>  When to use colour [possible values: auto, always, never]
  -h, --help           Print help
  -V, --version        Print version

Help topics:
  large-files  What happens to big files, and what to do about them

Run `paper help <topic>` to read one, or `paper help <command>` for a command.
